# Our generated double-ring rather than baresip's spoken ring.wav. A bare name
# here would be resolved against audio_path, so it is absolute -- and a
# pathname rather than the pinned-descriptor form used for the config
# directory, because baresip opens this one lazily, when a call arrives, and
# that would make the ring depend on an inherited descriptor surviving for the
# whole life of the process. The directory is 0700 and ownership-checked, and
# the worst a swapped file can do is play the wrong sound.
